WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Zero kara kakedashite

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Start running from the beginning,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
Omoi dake wo dakishimete

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
with nothing but your emotions in your hands.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Sonomama kakenukete

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Just keep running...

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
Itsumo koko de mitsumeteru

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
I'm always watching you from here.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
Hajimete deatta hi no manazashi wasurenai

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
I still remember your expression the day we first met.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
Taiyou mitai ni kokoro wo terashitekureta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
It lit up my heart like the sun.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
Asu no yukue sagashite nayandeiru nara

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
If you're anxious about where to go tomorrow,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
Ima kimi no tame ni akari ni naritai yo

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
I want to become a beacon to you.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Zero kara tobidatte

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Start flying from the beginning.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Ima no kimi wo toki hanachi

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Let go of your current self...

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
Mugen ni habataite

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
and fly towards infinity.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Donna toki mo mimaru yo

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
I will always watch over you...

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
Kitto zutto tooku made

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
no matter how far you fly.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 30 - A Million Rainbows

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:41.160
Spit it out!

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.000
You're unbelievable.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.260
I can't believe she actually ate those balls of mud!

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.420
She ate them because she's Toki.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.020
Ayumi!

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:57.310
If it had been any other girl, the play would have been ruined.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:59.010
You should be grateful.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:04.460
She ate those balls of mud because she knew...

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:07.740
the scene was necessary for the play to progress.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.800
She's frightening.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:13.700
The play's over,

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.800
but I still feel all warm inside.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.180
I'm off stage now, but I can still feel Toki inside me.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.470
For a moment, I forgot everything: I forgot who I was...

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.430
I forgot all my problems and my sorrows.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:34.090
Toki is still here inside me: she's in my hands and my feet and my whole body!

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:39.030
This was my very last play.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:47.760
Am I really going to let myself return to my old worthless self and live the rest of my life like that?

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.860
No!

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:53.070
I want to perform again!

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.850
I finally understand how much I love acting.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.690
But, what am I going to do?

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:03.100
No company will have me now!

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.300
Look at Ayumi.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.610
We're supposed to be competitors for the role of the Scarlet Angel...

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:11.040
but she's in a different league now.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.300
I'm waiting.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.150
She's waiting.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:28.350
She's waiting for the day when we can compete against each other...

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.010
for the role of the Scarlet Angel.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:33.350
She still believed in me.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.920
Even when everyone else had abandoned all hope,

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:39.230
she still understood my passion for acting.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:41.890
Wait for me!

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:44.100
Ayumi, please wait for me!

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.850
I will catch up to you!

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:57.030
And how exactly do you plan on doing that in your present state?

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:58.970
That's none of your business!

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.880
It's not like I was asking for your help.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.180
Here's your contract as promised.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:04.850
Wait.

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:10.290
If you leave Daito now, you'll never be able to get up on stage again.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.810
Well? Won't you at least consider it?

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:16.280
I was going to rip this contract up when you gave it to me.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.350
But will you rip it up for me instead?

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.690
Good answer.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.330
There you go.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:27.580
I'm setting you free, but only on the condition that you get in this car.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:34.430
Welcome back, Maya!

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:35.300
Hi everyone!

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.300
Miss Mizuki dropped your things off this afternoon.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.120
Miss Mizuki did that?

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.560
Was she wrong to do that?

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.280
Not at all!

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.580
Maya, I'm really sorry about what happened before.

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:47.830
It was all a misunderstanding.

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.230
We hope we can make up somehow.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.270
Thank you!

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:58.390
I remembered something important because you put me on stage today.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:04:59.830
Thank you!

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:02.560
I think that's the first time you've ever thanked me.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.820
What a kind smile...

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:13.990
Ms. Tsukikage!

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:16.780
I came to see you rehearsing for your next play.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.970
Maya's back, ma'am!

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:25.970
Please, ma'am... I'd really like to act here again!

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.970
I'll rehearse harder than I ever have before.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.420
So please, I really want to act with everyone again.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:31.890
Whether they forgive you or not is irrelevant.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.640
I will not forgive you.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:38.750
Maya, I put you into the care of Daito Entertainment, the hands of my nemesis,

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:42.190
to toughen you up and show you the outside world.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.700
As an agency, Daito is world class.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.890
Which is why I put you in the care of Mr. Hayami!

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:49.900
Ma'am...

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:54.150
I can't put you in a show now that you've been exiled from the acting world...

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:56.460
Not without jeopardizing everyone else.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.930
If you want to appear in a show performed by the Tsukikage Acting Troupe,

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:01.150
you'll have to clear your name first!

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.300
But, how can I do that?

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.060
You have to find that out for yourself.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:08.520
I'd like to see how you do it, too.

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:13.500
You want to join the Theater Club?

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:16.020
But we don't recruit new members halfway through the year.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.450
Nor do we accept any pros who have appeared on TV or in movies.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:21.560
Oh. I see.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.640
I'm surprised she had the guts to come back.

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:27.730
I can't believe she thinks she can look down on our Theater Club,

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:30.010
just because they kicked her out of a TV show!

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:31.860
I'm not going to let this get me down!

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.060
I will find a way in!

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.840
I'm really sorry!

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:42.530
No, I'm sorry. I was so absorbed in my book that I wasn't really paying attention.

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:44.850
"Bianca"?

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.520
What's it about?

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:51.730
It's a story about a princess who becomes a pirate.

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:56.040
"The name's Bianca Castiagni!"

00:06:56.040 --> 00:07:00.600
"I dresses like a man, but in fact, I be a woman."

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:04.050
"Oh yeah!"

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:05.610
"Hello boys!"

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.280
She's really good.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:15.070
I wonder what she's going to do next.

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.630
So, what am I doing now?

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:22.640
You're riding a bike!

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:30.600
I see. So, Maya's found a new tutor.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:34.460
It's hard to get children to understand what you're miming...

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:37.190
with just a single pose.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:41.430
If a child can understand what's being acted out, then anyone can understand it.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:47.280
I'm excited to see what she's going to do next.

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:52.370
School Festival Executives

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:51.630
Anyone wishing to participate in the festival should apply here!

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:02.410
I guess these belong to the P.E. Department.

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:09.110
I've never used one of these before!

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:14.600
"Me name is Bianca Castiagni!"

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:17.890
You want to put on the story of Bianca as a one-woman show?

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:18.970
But that's insane!

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.100
There are over thirty characters in that story!

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:25.380
But it can be done, if everything becomes a monologue by Bianca.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.010
Do you know anyone who can rewrite the script like that?

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:32.930
There's one guy in the Literature Club called Yoshizawa who might be able to do it.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.910
This is the only area we can use.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:39.040
I thought we could use all this stuff as pieces of the set.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.710
You want to use this stuff?

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:43.180
You really think you can put on a play in a place like this?

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:46.500
I'm sorry, but I don't think I'm about to rewrite this script.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:50.350
We asked you specifically because we know that you're the only guy for the job!

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:53.330
And if you try to weasel out of it, I'll have no choice but to report to the school governors...

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:56.570
that you've lost countless valuable books. It's my duty as the student librarian, after all.

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:59.120
Okay, okay, I'll do it!

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:01.710
But, are you really going to be able to do this all by yourself?

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:08.100
I'll do it. I have to do it or I won't make any headway.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:11.540
So, what's this I hear? Maya Kitajima's doing a one-woman play in the culture festival?

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:12.190
Yeah.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.590
I hear she's already registered.

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:16.880
How am I going to create this set?

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:20.050
It has to be made in such a way that the whole audience can see it.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:23.820
I see. It's hard putting on a play by yourself.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:29.270
There's no-one around to work on the props or the costumes, the lighting nor the directing,

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:31.810
let alone anyone to rehearse with.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:34.360
She's doing a one-woman show?

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:38.420
Well, I'm not coaching Maya this time.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:39.870
The audience will fulfill that role.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:41.100
The audience?

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:45.220
Yes. She's starting to understand too.

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:48.350
The best tutors you can get are the members of the audience.

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:51.480
The audience members are the best tutors?

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.460
You'll see soon enough.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:01.950
One Star Academy School Festival

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.450
I heard that the Theater Club's <i>Faust</i> cast have done a great job on their set and costumes!

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:07.470
Let's go see it!

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:11.120
One-Woman Show: Maya Kitajima
<i>Pirate Queen Bianca</i>

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:11.510
Don't you want to see what kind of show she's gonna put on?

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:13.360
You know, that girl who's been cast out of the acting world.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:14.890
You only want to see it because of that, don't you?

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.500
There's all sorts of people here.

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:21.010
They're mostly hecklers.

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:23.880
I see! This choice of venue means people will get up...

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:25.310
and leave immediately if it starts getting boring.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:27.430
Oh, you've come too?

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:28.870
Ma'am!

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:32.450
I'm here today as an ordinary spectator.

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:34.810
The show's about to start!

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:49.000
The year is 1523.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:54.670
A single pirate vessel has been captured by Genova's fleet in the western region...

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:57.420
of the Italian Mediterranean Sea.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:02.550
All pirates on board have been sentenced to be executed.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:05.550
That's meant to be the deck?

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:12.010
What's this? The soldiers are crying out that there's a woman disguised as a pirate!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:17.340
Get yer hands off me!

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:21.940
Wow - she transformed into a pirate in a flash.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:25.980
All o' ye aboard this ship today!

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:27.970
Ms. Tsukikage?

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:32.980
The name's Nicolo. But me real name's Bianca Castiagni.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:37.370
I be the daughter of a high-and-mighty Venetian aristocrat who took up arms against Genova.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:39.470
So, you wanna know why...

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:41.430
I disguised meself as a man and stand before ye in the garb of a pirate?

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:46.300
I lost me ma when I was eight...

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:49.340
and from then on, nursemaids were draconian in raisin' me.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:56.230
But I always preferred the way of the sword to the hoity-toity life of an aristocrat!

00:11:56.230 --> 00:12:02.880
I tricked me nursemaids and spent all my free time in disguise, practicing swordplay with boys!

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:09.140
But even I harbored a young lass's dreams.

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:15.260
I dreamed of wearing frilly dresses and havin' love sweepin' me of me feet!

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:21.630
At thirteen, that dream was smashed to smithereens.

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:24.690
Me engagement was announced.

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:29.150
Me marriage was meant to finally bring peace between Venice and Genova.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:35.780
An' that's how I left Venice.

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:38.640
I were about to march into the underworld...

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:44.740
She's on a gondola now!

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:10.840
Hey, this is where Maya Kitajima's doing that one-woman show!

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:14.250
What the hell do they think they're doing?

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.810
They've completely destroyed the atmosphere!

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:18.990
Avast ye!

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:23.290
I be the daughter of Venetian nobility - the name's Bianca!

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:28.100
'Tis an honor to meet ye, Mister Ambassador.

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:35.390
'Tis truly an honor. Milord, me name's Bianca.

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:41.500
Her instincts kicked in before the illusion was destroyed.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.690
Her breathing and timing are so honed that she can focus...

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:46.750
the audience's attention from left to right in a flash.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:51.130
The audience is honing her skills.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:56.280
It's now time to meet me fiancé Lorenzo.

00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:59.230
The door opens.

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:02.290
An' he's a sight, let me tell ye.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:03.840
This man were gonna be...

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:08.700
Master Lorenzo!

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:14.970
Bianca, I promise to love you and be by your side for the rest of my days.

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:20.000
Our union will bring peace, understanding and love to both our regions!

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:23.280
A one-woman show in the P.E. storeroom?

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:25.260
Sounds like a shabby affair.

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:28.140
So, she's finally back on her feet.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.550
I can't let my guard down.

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:35.270
We come from very different backgrounds, but I understand her.

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:39.380
Our mutual passion for acting makes her closer to me...

00:14:39.380 --> 00:14:42.080
than anyone else in the whole world.

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:45.670
You are always there, trailing me.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:48.200
I'm waiting for you, Maya.

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:51.260
Bianca swore to honor Lorenzo in marriage,

00:14:51.260 --> 00:15:00.220
but a rival country's plot implicated her as the murderer of Lorenzo's elder sister.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:09.500
But Master Lorenzo... I be innocent!

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:16.040
I'll disguise meself as a man and run off to Greece!

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:18.040
I'll cut me hair and wield a sword!

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:21.320
Farewell, Venice!

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:25.960
I beg ye, burn me love and me memories and everything I have!

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:32.010
Till not even ash remains.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:57.110
Maya's doing a one-woman show!

00:15:57.110 --> 00:15:57.910
Oh?

00:15:57.910 --> 00:15:59.020
Aren't you going to go see her?

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:01.010
I don't have time for such things.

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:04.510
I'll leave these for you then.

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:08.000
One Star Academy School Festival

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:11.440
That was great!

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:12.250
Bianca!

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:13.220
You did it!

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:15.390
I didn't think you could manage all that by yourself!

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:21.390
It's as though she's made everyone forget about the scandals surrounding her.

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:24.390
Thank you, thank you!

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:26.980
I can do this! I know I can!

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:28.650
I'm going to be able to act again!

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:31.620
Why are they ignoring us because of her?

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:39.630
The show was so popular with the students that they requested a second performance.

00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:42.630
So, they've asked for another showing?

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:45.380
I'm proud of you, Maya.

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:47.620
Now, make sure you don't let anyone down.

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:48.980
Thank you, Ma'am!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.850
There were a few issues I noticed, however.

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:53.230
Ma'am...

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:55.840
You need to pay attention to your breathing.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:59.730
I counted seven separate occasions where you breathed in while speaking.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:04.720
In Scene Thirteen, right after your dance with Lorenzo, you need to leave a beat!

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:07.590
You need to pause to let your expression of love sink in!

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:11.130
You must never forget about your audience.

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:15.470
The audience members are the very reason an actor even exists.

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:22.050
They can teach you a very important lesson, because their reactions are honest.

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:24.060
You must never forget that!

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:29.380
Ma'am, please! Tutor me again like you used to!

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:31.140
Please give me acting lessons!

00:17:31.140 --> 00:17:34.290
You're the only one who can make yourself grow.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:37.020
You take what is necessary from your own self!

00:17:37.850 --> 00:17:40.640
I will always be watching you, though.

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:42.140
Both you and Ayumi.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.950
The Passing Rain

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:46.970
I think this might be good.

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:52.110
But it's a story about a regular high school girl!

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:53.730
Isn't that too boring for a play?

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:58.340
I want to do a regular, everyday story because it'd push my acting skills to their limits.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:01.320
I want to try it.

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:05.240
A regular household with a father who works in an office, a mother who's good in the kitchen,

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:09.230
an older brother and a younger sister.

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.310
And the incident that rocks their world.

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:16.430
We will be talking about the first ever attempt to enact <i>Romeo and Juliet</i> as a one-woman show, without Romeo.

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:19.320
That's quite a difficult approach towards Shakespeare.

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:23.610
I am not in fact challenging <i>Romeo and Juliet</i>.

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:26.190
I am making Juliet a challenge for myself.

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:32.240
What does Juliet feel? What does she think? What does she do...

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:34.810
when she falls in love with a boy called Romeo?

00:18:35.200 --> 00:18:38.740
And what is she willing to sacrifice for love?

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:42.340
This is a play that will focus solely on Juliet.

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:40.880
Wait!

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:43.690
Rei!

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:46.470
Take a look at this cup.

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:50.170
Even when you put it down, your hand should still hang in the air for a moment.

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:51.940
Try it again.

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:57.430
"All right. It's breakfast time!"

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.470
Ma'am!

00:19:03.970 --> 00:19:07.510
Will you please watch me rehearse for just a little while?

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:11.650
I'm not confident enough and I keep wondering what I need to do...

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:14.560
for the audience to understand me!

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:18.140
You're finally thinking about your audience.

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:20.050
Get on the bus.

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:22.490
Yes, ma'am!

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:27.800
Now, a train.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:35.470
Stop.

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:38.960
Buses and trains jolt about in a different way, don't they?

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:42.470
I hadn't noticed that until I tried miming it just now.

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:45.550
Well, your body has memorized the movements.

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:47.050
It has?

00:19:47.050 --> 00:19:48.330
What's important...

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:51.800
is remembering that each member of the audience is also watching with their own memories.

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:55.760
Audience members watch with their own memories...

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:59.350
Your acting needs to come from the heart, Maya.

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:03.870
Ma'am!

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:05.300
Keep rehearsing!

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:06.500
Ma'am!

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:12.420
Maya, the success of one show raises the curtain of the next one.

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:16.590
And at the end of that trail of plays is <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>!

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:24.050
I wonder if she's actually going back to the hospital like she's supposed to...

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:27.880
Why did you call me?

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:30.020
I'm a pretty heartless guy,

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:33.180
so I can't promise that I'll even listen to whatever it is you have to say.

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:34.890
That's your opinion of me, isn't it?

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:37.480
Well, I...

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:40.180
Why am I calling Masumi Hayami?

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:43.740
I guess it's because I couldn't think of anyone else to call.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:44.880
But that means...

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:48.730
I'm glad you're keeping me in your thoughts.

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:56.760
I'm fine.

00:20:57.030 --> 00:21:01.510
You think I'm going to die before I get to see <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> again?

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:05.310
You live for that alone, don't you?

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:07.530
Correct.

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:10.630
It's what I was born to do.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:14.210
And now, I am living for <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> once again.

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:20.180
But why are you so hung up on <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>?

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:23.980
Because it's been my father's dream to put on that piece ever since he was young.

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:29.000
And I will use any means necessary to acquire the rights to that play.

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:31.100
The only reason I don't do that now...

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:34.170
is because the person I face is you, the Scarlet Angel herself.

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:39.300
Keep going, you two.

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:43.400
Fight for the part and find out which one of you will finally get the role.

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:47.860
And then, carry on my legacy!

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
Chikazukitai noni toozaketeshimau

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
I want to be close to you, but you're distancing yourself.

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
Dakishimetai toki wazato hanareteshimau

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
When I want to hold you, you deliberately run away.

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
Marude jishaku no N to N no you da ne

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
We're like two poles on a magnet...

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Otagai amari nimo nisugita seikana?

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Maybe we're too alike?

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
Motto motto sunao na hitomi de mitsureba

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
If you allow your eyes to see the truth,

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
Yodonderu izumi mo suki tooru hazusa

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
even quagmires will become crystal clear.

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:26.750
My time is running out, minute by minute.

00:23:27.850 --> 00:23:32.020
You're finally back on your feet, Maya...

00:23:32.020 --> 00:23:35.200
but look at how much further ahead Ayumi is now.

00:23:35.630 --> 00:23:40.240
You won't catch up to her unless you start running!

00:23:41.080 --> 00:23:42.880
This isn't the time for tears.

00:23:43.280 --> 00:23:46.670
Run onward and don't look away!

00:23:46.330 --> 00:23:51.580
Episode 31 - The One-Woman Show

00:23:47.010 --> 00:23:51.590
Neither of us has a moment to lose!
